  "question": {
    "text": "The area of the region bounded by the curve \\(y=x|x|, x\\)-axis and the ordinates \\(x=1, x=-1\\) is given by :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "D4SGO",
      "text": "zero",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rN5jA",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "09myO",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MMNBZ",
      "text": "1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The area of the region bounded by the curve \\(y=f(x)\\) and the ordinates \\(x=a, x=b\\) is given by\n\\(\\text {Area }=\\left|\\int_a^b y d x\\right|\\)\nAccording to the question,\n\\(y=x|x|= \\begin{cases}x^2, & x \\geq 0 \\\\ -x^2, & x  < 0\\end{cases}\\)<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/FZCw9yBYXriAVn3LRBhGUGiFnLoUl_9mYiLSqNxNlqc.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nRequired area\n\\(=\\) area of region \\(\\mathrm{OAB}+\\) area of region \\(\\mathrm{OCD}\\)\n\\(=2 \\times\\) Area of region \\(\\mathrm{OAB}\\)\n\\(=2 \\int_0^1 x^2 d x=\\frac{2}{3} s q\\). units",
    "image": null
  },
